Now, before we go away on the break, though,

152
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:17,300
I want to take some time and talk about

153
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:19,000
the future of scouting, and that's going to

154
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,700
take up the remainder of the podcast.

155
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:23,400
So let's get started, shall we?

156
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:56,300
So what is the future of scouting?

157
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:58,500
I mean, we're busy people, right,

158
00:07:58,500 --> 00:07:59,600
Scouters are busy people.

159
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:01,300
We may not have a whole lot of time to sit

160
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:04,800
down and think through what the future is

161
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:06,700
going to be like, but I think it's an

162
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:09,600
interesting question to ask, and I'll

163
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:11,700
start off by saying I'm thoroughly

164
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,400
optimistic about the future of scouting.

165
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:15,400
Scouting's been around for more than

166
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,400
a century now.

167
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,900
It is such an inherently human endeavor

168
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:21,900
I think it will survive and thrive

169
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:24,500
and remain relevant where people value

170
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:27,400
and understand what it does for young

171
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:27,800
people.

172
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:30,000
Our future is going to be partially

173
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,500
defined by our past, isn't it?

174
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:33,400
I mean, we have to understand what

175
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:35,400
scouting is and a little bit about

176
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:38,299
our own history before we can project

177
00:08:38,299 --> 00:08:41,200
into the future and begin to get an idea

178
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,799
of what things will be like.

179
00:08:42,799 --> 00:08:44,200
And when I say scouting here,

180
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:45,400
I'm not talking about a particular

181
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:46,200
organization.

182
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:48,200
Organizations are very mercurial.

183
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:50,600
Scouting is just what it is.

184
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,800
It's an idea, and the organizations

185
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:54,200
that we've formed to contain that

186
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:56,400
idea. well, they can change,

187
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:58,400
They can come and go, but scouting

188
00:08:58,400 --> 00:08:59,699
will continue on.

189
00:08:59,699 --> 00:09:01,900
And when you boil things down,

190
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:04,000
scouting is very, very simple.

191
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,600
We have one aim, and that is to develop

192
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:09,000
character in young people, and one method,

193
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,600
and that is the patrol method.

194
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:13,100
Everything else, everything else,

195
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:15,400
is just window dressing, really,

196
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:17,300
And I know that sounds like a vast

197
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:19,400
oversimplification, but think about

198
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:20,199
this for a moment.

199
00:09:20,199 --> 00:09:21,699
Imagine you're taking scouting to

200
00:09:21,699 --> 00:09:23,300
young people anywhere in the world,

201
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:26,500
Absent any big organization,

202
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:28,900
absent any resources at all.

203
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:31,900
The whole thing is going to be

204
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,900
about developing character

205
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:36,300
in young people by applying

206
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:37,500
the patrol method.

207
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:38,800
Doesn't matter what you call

208
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:40,200
the small group of young people

209
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:41,100
that you're working with.

210
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:42,100
you can call it a patrol,

211
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:43,100
you can call it a Dan,

212
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:44,900
you can call it a crew, whatever

213
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:46,700
It's. still, those concepts

214
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:48,800
are going to be in play and boiled

215
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:50,900
down to its basic essentials.

216
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:52,300
That's what scouting is:

217
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:54,600
Developing character in young people

218
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,800
through applying the patrol method.

219
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:58,800
I mean, character is the essence

220
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:00,800
of good citizenship, isn't it

221
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:03,500
An ideal good citizen

222
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:06,200
would benefit from and contribute

223
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:08,100
to the society in which they live?

224
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:08,700
right,

225
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:11,100
The most human thing we can do

226
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:13,100
is to look out for somebody else,

227
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:14,700
to put their well-being

228
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:16,300
above that of our own,

229
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:18,400
And the ideal of goodwill

230
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:20,100
and family, expanded

231
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:21,900
beyond our own self-interest,

232
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:25,300
is at the heart of scouting.

233
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:27,500
So in this work of developing character

234
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:28,600
in young people

235
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:30,100
through the patrol method,

236
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:33,300
we balance two very important things.

237
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:34,199
And to shed a little light

238
00:10:34,199 --> 00:10:35,600
on what I mean by that,

239
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:37,699
I want to go back to 1922,

240
00:10:37,699 --> 00:10:39,300
where Baden Powell spoke

241
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:41,400
to the Third International Congress

242
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:43,300
of Moral Education

243
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:44,900
in Geneva, Switzerland,

244
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:46,800
And the title of his address

245
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:49,500
was Education in Love

246
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:51,199
in Place of Fear.

247
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:52,900
What a great title, huh?

248
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:55,500
I mean, that was 94 years ago

249
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:57,800
and I'll bet you didn't realize

250
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:58,800
that Baden Powell

251
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:01,600
was one of the first hippies.

252
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:02,800
I mean: education in love

253
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:03,600
in place of fear.

254
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:05,300
What an interesting concept.

255
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:06,600
So it's 1922.

256
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:07,600
It's in the aftermath

257
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:09,100
of the First World War

258
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:11,500
And Baden Powell goes to speak

259
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:13,000
about scouting

260
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,600
as a movement

261
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:16,400
for world peace.

262
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:18,500
And Baden Powell's argument

263
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:19,400
in that address

264
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,800
was that scouting,

265
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:22,600
when properly understood and applied,

266
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:26,000
balanced two inherently human tendencies

267
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,700
to foster peaceful cooperation.

268
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:29,700
In his address

269
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:32,700
he quoted British educator Edmund Holmes

270
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:34,400
who said the scout movement

271
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:35,500
owes its success

272
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:37,200
to the fact that it makes

273
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:39,500
due provision for the satisfaction

274
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:41,700
of two imperious needs

275
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:44,000
of human nature:

276
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
The need to realize one's own self

277
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,300
and the need to work with

278
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:51,000
and for others.

279
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
In the scout philosophy of education

280
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,400
the balance between the claims

281
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,900
of the individual

282
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:57,900
and of the communal self

283
00:11:57,900 --> 00:12:00,000
is steadily maintained.

284
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,100
To achieve and maintain this balance

285
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:03,600
should be the primary aim

286
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:04,800
of all

287
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:06,600
who are interested in education.

288
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,100
So scouting balances

289
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:11,000
what Holmes called these

290
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,200
two imperious needs

291
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:15,100
of man's nature:

292
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:16,900
to realize one's own self

293
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,800
and the need to work with

294
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,100
and for others.

295
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:21,699
And when you balance those two things

296
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:22,300
what do you have?

297
00:12:22,300 --> 00:12:24,300
You have peace, cooperation.

298
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:25,800
I think if you kind of

299
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:27,300
look over the last century of scouting

300
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:29,800
and think about your own scouting experiences,

301
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:30,800
I think we can agree

302
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:32,600
that scouting goes awry

303
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:33,900
when its use is limited

304
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:35,600
to self-development

305
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:37,500
or a method of education

306
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,699
or a leadership school.

307
00:12:39,699 --> 00:12:41,699
I mean, our aim is definitely

308
00:12:41,699 --> 00:12:43,100
helping an individual

309
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:45,000
develop character right,

310
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,600
But that is kind of

311
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:50,000
wrapped in this interesting paradox.

312
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,300
We develop individual character

313
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:54,500
by balancing your individual needs

314
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:56,300
against the needs

315
00:12:56,300 --> 00:12:58,000
of the broader group,

316
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,100
the broader community.

317
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:00,000
And we do that,

318
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
beginning in the patrol,

319
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,900
because we understand

320
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:06,600
that the greatest benefit

321
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:09,100
of the service we render to others

322
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:11,300
is what we derive ourselves

323
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:12,900
from that service.

324
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:15,199
That's kind of hard to get sometimes,

325
00:13:15,199 --> 00:13:17,400
because scouting is not about

326
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:19,900
developing yourself exclusively,

327
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:20,900
It's about

328
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:23,500
serving the welfare of others.

329
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:25,600
So if scouting just becomes

330
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:28,699
like a merit badge delivery system

331
00:13:28,699 --> 00:13:31,699
or a leadership development school,

332
00:13:31,699 --> 00:13:33,900
if we just focus on those

333
00:13:33,900 --> 00:13:35,699
very limited aspects of things,

334
00:13:35,699 --> 00:13:37,199
we miss the mark.

335
00:13:37,199 --> 00:13:39,800
If we invest in,

336
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:41,000
I don't know, just having

337
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,500
all kinds of grand events

338
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:45,200
or cutting edge facilities

339
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:48,300
or just over-emphasized

340
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:49,800
learning, the skills of the outdoors,

341
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,900
all of these elements of scouting

342
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:54,800
that work very well together. in isolation

343
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:56,100
they kind of throw the balance

344
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:57,800
of everything off.

345
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:00,300
So what is the future of scouting?

346
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:02,700
That's where we started, right.

347
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:04,500
So if you think about this,

348
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:05,800
when we speak about the future

349
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:08,100
we talk in terms of technology,

350
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:09,200
and no doubt technology

351
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:11,100
will have a big role in shaping our future.

352
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:13,300
but there's more than technology

353
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:14,900
to think about, because

354
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:17,200
our future is also going to be defined

355
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:18,700
by the way we relate to each other

356
00:14:18,700 --> 00:14:20,400
and the path that our lives take

357
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:22,900
and that is shaped by the content

358
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:24,200
of our character,

359
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:25,500
and that aspect of humanity

360
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:27,500
will always shape our future.

361
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:29,200
So scouting remains relevant.

362
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:30,500
We form the character

363
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,000
that forms the future.

364
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,600
Now I'm tempted to say something like

365
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,300
in these troubled times

366
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:37,500
and things like that.

367
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:38,600
but look,

368
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:40,900
if you take the past century

369
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:42,500
and you don't just focus on scouting

370
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:44,300
but you look at the broader things

371
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:45,300
that are going on in the world,

372
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:47,000
there's always been instability

373
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:47,800
and troubled times.

374
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:49,500
I mean, there's been two world wars

375
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:51,400
and there's been all kinds

376
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:53,600
of cultural upheavals

377
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:56,400
and socioeconomic upheavals

378
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:57,600
and political upheavals

379
00:14:57,600 --> 00:14:58,600
and things like that.

380
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:01,000
and what gives me confidence

381
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,100
in the future

382
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:03,900
is the consistency

383
00:15:03,900 --> 00:15:06,500
and the reliability of the concepts

384
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:08,700
that underlie the scouting movement.

385
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:11,000
So my outlook is optimistic

386
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,300
and pro-topian.

387
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:15,100
So there's a word you might not have heard before:

388
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:16,400
pro-topian.

389
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:17,400
It's an interesting word

390
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:18,700
that I believe was coined

391
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:20,400
by the author Kevin Kelly.

392
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:22,100
Kevin Kelly is always on my reading list.

393
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:24,200
If you aren't familiar with Kevin's work,

394
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:26,200
his latest book is titled

395
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:28,100
The Inevitable Twelve Trends

396
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:29,300
That Will Shape Our Future,

397
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:31,300
and I'll throw a link to it

398
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:32,400
in the podcast notes

399
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:34,800
if that kind of thing's interest you.

400
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:36,400
But here's what Kevin has to say

401
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:38,300
about pro-topia.

402
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:40,300
Pro-topia is a state

403
00:15:40,300 --> 00:15:42,000
that is better today

404
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,600
than yesterday,

405
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:45,600
although it might only be a little better-

406
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:50,800
And so pro-topia

407
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:52,800
is middle ground

408
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:54,400
to utopia

409
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:55,800
and dystopia.

410
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:58,199
So we're not headed towards utopia,

411
00:15:58,199 --> 00:16:00,800
where everything is sweetness and light,

412
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:03,100
and we're not headed toward dystopia.

413
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:04,199
It's more realistic

414
00:16:04,199 --> 00:16:06,100
and measured to say that

415
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:08,300
our future is pro-topian,

416
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:12,300
And that idea is a little harder to visualize

417
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:14,400
because there are as many problems

418
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:16,100
as benefits in the future

419
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:18,700
and the complex interaction of working

420
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:21,100
and broken, as Kevin Kelly says,

421
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:22,900
is very hard to predict.

422
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:24,500
And I don't know.

423
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:25,500
there was just something

424
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:27,000
in the definition of that term

425
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,900
that I really identified with scouting,

426
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:32,900
because we have this utopian set of goals

427
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:34,300
set in front of us

428
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:36,800
and we know that we have good things happen.

429
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:38,000
We have bad things happen,

430
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,200
We have an inherent level of chaos

431
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:41,800
dealing with young people,

432
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:43,200
But it gives me hope to think

433
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:45,000
in terms of pro-topia,

434
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,400
because that means

435
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:48,000
that tomorrow needs to be

436
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,900
just a little bit better than today.

437
00:16:51,100 --> 00:16:52,900
It doesn't have to be utopia.

438
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:55,600
We may lose a little ground now and again,

439
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:57,400
but the general trend,

440
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:58,600
things are getting better.

441
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,200
And listen, I know that we all look

442
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,000
for some kind of assurance

443
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,900
that our future is going to be

444
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:07,900
even remotely positive,

445
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:09,900
and that kind of assurance

446
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:12,400
can be very difficult to find

447
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:15,599
in the cycle of endlessly bad news

448
00:17:15,599 --> 00:17:17,400
that we seem to be steeped in

449
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:19,000
from day to day to day.

450
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,300
If you're going to pay attention

451
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:20,900
to the news

452
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:23,000
you're probably going to be discouraged.

453
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,300
But if you look at the young people

454
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:26,099
you're working with and scouting,

455
00:17:26,099 --> 00:17:28,300
I think that lightens things up a little.

456
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:29,600
I mean, look at the promise

457
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:31,500
and potential there.

458
00:17:31,500 --> 00:17:33,900
Aim at the heart of the matter

459
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:35,800
and give these young people

460
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:36,800
your best effort.

461
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:37,900
Don't allow the negatives

462
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:39,800
in the world to define your outlook.

463
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:41,700
Look at the potential

464
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:42,600
in the young people

465
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:43,600
that you're working with.

466
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:44,600
The future of scouting

467
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:46,300
is bright and relevant

468
00:17:46,300 --> 00:17:48,600
so long as we understand

469
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:49,800
what it is

470
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:51,200
and we apply it

471
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,600
with a lot of optimism.

472
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:55,200
because scouting is much greater

473
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:56,200
than a hedge

474
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:58,100
against the perilous future

475
00:17:58,100 --> 00:18:00,900
or a return to a storied past

476
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:02,500
that never existed.

477
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:05,400
It's a transformative

478
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:07,200
individual journey

479
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:09,800
following the scout oath and law,

480
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:12,400
very direct statements

481
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:14,000
of the virtues and obligations

482
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,100
that have defined stable,

483
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:17,200
enlightened societies

484
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,600
throughout human history.

485
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:20,900
That's our pro-topian future

486
00:18:20,900 --> 00:18:21,900
in scouting.

487
00:18:21,900 --> 00:18:23,300
That's what we

488
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:25,300
scouters get to make happen.

489
00:18:25,300 --> 00:18:26,800
one scout at a time

490
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:28,100
Isn't that great.

491
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:29,500
So let's go out

492
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:30,900
and get with the program

493
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:31,900
and give it our best.

